.TH "SPGEN-CONTROLLER" "1" "" "spgen 0.1.0" ""
.SH NAME
spgen\-controller \- Generates the controller action, endpoint test and route
.SH SYNOPSIS
mix sp.gen.controller [options] <COMMAND|QUERY>
.SH DESCRIPTION
The HTTP adapter for one operation: parse the request, call the public API (../domain/public\-api.md), render the response. No domain logic — the public API is the only thing a controller may call.
.SH Prerequisite
.IP \[bu] 2
The Domain Model (../../../../domain\-model/README.md) contains the command or query.
.IP \[bu] 2
The public API function, the view (./view.md) and the schemas (./schema.md) exist — until they do, the action defers and the run reports skipped: spgen public_api, skipped: spgen schema, …
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/lib/sportipedia_web/router.ex exists. It is operator\-owned and merge\-only: a missing router is a Failed, not something the generator invents.
.SH "What the generator does"
.IP \[bu] 2
The controller module with use SportipediaWeb, :controller, use OpenApiSpex.ControllerSpecs, the Bodyguard.Plug.Authorize plug on the constituent's policy with SportipediaWeb.System.FallbackController, and tags ["<composite>"].
.IP \[bu] 2
One action per operation, operation :<op> with summary, request body and responses (including the shared not_found / unprocessable_entity / unauthorized / forbidden references), a @spec, and the action body for the effect: create, update and read render the resource as ok:, a collection renders index.json, delete and archive send no_content (204).
.IP \[bu] 2
For a collection query, the JSONAPI.QueryParser plug: filter: from the model's parameters.filter.properties, sort: from its sortableFields (the filterable fields when it names none), view: the constituent's view — the same two lists the query parameters schema (./schema.md) documents, gated on the view.
.IP \[bu] 2
The route in the web router's scope chain (/<subdomain> → /<composite> → /<domain\-object>s), materializing missing scope levels. Only GET for queries and POST for commands — every write is a command endpoint, so there is no PATCH/PUT/DELETE route.
.PP
@moduledoc and @doc come from the model; OpenAPI summaries fall back to a TODO: marker.
.PP
The boundary is absolute: a controller calls the public API (../domain/public\-api.md) and nothing else — never Repo, never a query, never an aggregate. A response the operation does not imply starts in the domain model, not in this file.
.SH Tests
The endpoint test is contributed by this same run; see Endpoint Test (./endpoint\-test.md).
.SH Learnings
.SS "Finding: 200 or 201 for a create endpoint"
.SS "DO NOT"
Copy put_status(:created) and a created: response from the existing equipment controllers and call it the standard.
.SS "DO INSTEAD"
200 is the standard: this blueprint and SpGen.Blueprint.Controller answer ok: (200) for a create, and a generated controller and its generated test agree on it. catalog/equipment/apparatus and instrument answer 201 — legacy, decided against, not a pattern to copy or to re\-litigate per slice; moving them is a follow\-up (../../../../follow\-ups.md#equipment\-create\-endpoints\-move\-to\-200).
.SS "Generated files"
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/lib/sportipedia_web/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/<domain_object>_controller.ex (endpoint action calling the API)
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/test/sportipedia_web/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/operations/<_operation>_endpoint_test.exs (request response endpoint tests)
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/lib/sportipedia_web/router.ex (authenticated scope route)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-subdomain\fR \fI<SUBDOMAIN>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-composite\fR \fI<COMPOSITE>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-constituent\fR \fI<CONSTITUENT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
model root, default docs/domain\-model (relative to \-\-root)
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR
repo root, default inferred from the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
report the drift, write nothing
.TP
\fB\-\-template\fR \fI<TEMPLATE>\fR
what the operation does: create|update|delete|none|read|collection (optional: the model declares the operation for this element)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
create
.IP \(bu 2
update
.IP \(bu 2
delete
.IP \(bu 2
none
.IP \(bu 2
read
.IP \(bu 2
collection
.RE
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
FE: rewrite present generated units in place
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fICOMMAND|QUERY\fR>
the element: esdm: reference, *.esdm.yaml, kind.name, or bare name
